@@ -101,6 +101,18 @@ Set `BASE_URL` to the full URL where your Fizzy instance is accessible:
 docker run --env BASE_URL=https://fizzy.example.com ...
 ```
 
+#### Web push notifications (optional)
+
+Fizzy can send each notification to the browsers and home screen apps where people have turned them on.
+To enable this, you need a VAPID key pair. Generate one once, and keep it somewhere safe:
+
+```sh
+docker run --rm <your-fizzy-image> ./bin/rails runner 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}", "VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{key.private_key}"'
+```
+
+Then set `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` to those values.
+People can turn notifications on for each device from their notification settings. If these variables are not set, that option is hidden.
+
 #### S3 storage (optional)
 
 If you'd prefer that uploaded files were stored in an S3 bucket rather than in your mounted volume, you can set that up.
diff --git a/docs/kamal-deployment.md b/docs/kamal-deployment.md
index 5dcd257..5a15b6d 100644
--- a/docs/kamal-deployment.md
+++ b/docs/kamal-deployment.md
@@ -57,6 +57,9 @@ The values you enter here will be specific to you, and you can get or create the
 
 - `SECRET_KEY_BASE` should be a long, random secret. You can run `bin/rails secret` to create a suitable value for this.
 - `SMTP_USERNAME` & `SMTP_PASSWORD` should be valid credentials for your SMTP server. If you're using a 3rd-party service here, consult their documentation for what to use.
+
+Web push notifications are optional. To turn them on, generate a VAPID key pair with `bin/rails runner 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts key.public_key, key.private_key'`, add `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` to `.kamal/secrets`, and list both under `env/secret` in `config/deploy.yml`.
+
 Once you've made all those changes, commit them to your fork so they're saved.
 
 ### Deploy Fizzy!
